      "SUBAWARD_DESCRIPTION": "SCOPE OF WORK\n \n \n CHARLES CASPER, PHD, STATISTICIAN, WILL DEVOTE 5% EFFORT. DR. CASPER WILL BE DIRECTLY INVOLVED IN THE DESIGN AND IMPLEMENTATION OF THE STUDY AND WILL SUPERVISE AND CONDUCT ANALYSIS OF THE STUDY DATA. HE WILL OVERSEE ALL ASPECTS OF THE STUDY AND COMMUNICATE WITH THE PRINCIPAL INVESTIGATOR REGULARLY.\n \n TBA DATA MANAGER WILL DEVOTE 35% EFFORT. THE DATA MANAGER WILL PARTICIPATE IN A MULTI-DISCIPLINARY TEAM OF STUDY PERSONNEL TO ASSIST STUDY PRINCIPAL INVESTIGATOR(S) IN ACCOMPLISHING STUDY OBJECTIVES. THIS POSITION WILL BUILD THE STUDY DATABASE, DEVELOP AND MANAGE DATA QUERIES, ASSESS DATA QUALITY AND COMMUNICATE WITH SITES REGARDING DATA ISSUES. THIS PERSON WILL ASSIST SITES IN TROUBLESHOOTING ISSUES RELATED TO DATA COLLECTION, DATA ENTRY AND QUERY RESOLUTION AND WILL PROVIDE INDIVIDUAL AND GROUP TRAINING ON DATA ENTRY SYSTEMS. \n \n TBA MS STATISTICIAN WILL DEVOTE 21% EFFORT. THE MASTER S STATISTICIAN WILL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR DESIGNING STUDY SPECIFIC STATISTICAL PLANS, ASSISTING INVESTIGATORS WITH STATISTICAL ASPECTS OF PROTOCOL DEVELOPMENT, AND PROVIDING STUDY SPECIFIC DATA REPORTS TO DEMONSTRATE STUDY PROGRESS.  THE STATISTICIAN ALSO WORKS CLOSELY WITH THE DATA MANAGER AND THE STUDY TEAM TO DEVELOP THE DATA ELEMENTS AND DATABASE TO REFLECT THE STUDY ANALYSES PLAN. THIS POSITION WILL ALSO PREPARE THE DATA SAFETY MONITORING BOARD (DSMB) REPORT AT REGULAR INTERVALS AS SPECIFIED BY THE PROTOCOL OR REQUESTED BY THE DSMB. THE STATISTICIAN WILL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR COMPLETING DATA ANALYSES FOR THE STUDY UNDER THE DIRECTION OF THE PHD STATISTICIAN. THIS STATISTICIAN WILL ALSO ASSIST DATA MANAGERS WITH EVALUATING DATA ELEMENTS AND WILL WORK WITH INVESTIGATORS ON MANUSCRIPT DEVELOPMENT. THIS POSITION WILL PARTICIPATE ON MULTI-DISCIPLINARY STUDY TEAMS AT THE DCC TO PROVIDE INPUT ON QUALITY OF DATA. \n \n TBA PROJECT MANAGER WILL DEVOTE 50% EFFORT. THE PROJECT MANAGER WILL DEVELOP THE MANUAL OF OPERATIONS, STUDY DOCUMENTS, AND PROVIDE TECHNICAL AND PROJECT MANAGEMENT SUPPORT TO PARTICIPATING SITES. THE COORDINATOR WILL PROVIDE TRACKING OF REGULATORY DOCUMENT AND ASSIST WITH DEVELOPMENT OF THE INFORMED CONSENT DOCUMENTS. THE COORDINATOR WILL ALSO ASSIST WITH TRAINING, AND COORDINATE SITE MONITORING DOCUMENTS. \n \n UTAH WILL CREATE TWO DATABASES: REDCAP AND OPENCLINICA. OPENCLINICA WILL INCLUDE DE-IDENTIFIED INFORMATION, WITH THE EXCEPTION OF VISIT DATES (PHI) AND REDCAP WILL CONTAIN PHI (CONTACT INFORMATION FOR ALL SUBJECTS) IN ORDER TO OBTAIN FOLLOW UP INFORMATION. BECAUSE THE STATISTICIAN IS LOCATED AT UTAH, THIS SITE WILL HAVE ACCESS TO ALL THE DATA FOR ALL THE SITES. UTAH WILL NOT BE INVOLVED IN INVOICING OR PAYMENT TO THE SUB SITES. THE PRIMARY SITE (WASH U) WILL MAINTAIN ENROLLMENT INFORMATION AND THE RC (RESEARCH COORDINATOR) WILL USE THAT INFORMATION TO PROCESS A REPORT THAT WILL BE USED TO CALCULATE AND ISSUE QUARTERLY PAYMENTS TO THE SUB-SITES. \n \n SITE MONITORING REQUIREMENT: ON-SITE AND REMOTE MONITORING AS BUDGETED. \n DETAILS ON DATA TRANSFER: PARTIALLY IDENTIFIABLE INFORMATION FOR ALL SITES WILL BE SENT TO AND MAINTAINED AT THE PECARN DATA COORDINATING CENTER LOCATED AT THE UNIVERSITY OF UTAH IN SALT LAKE CITY, UTAH. THE DATA COORDINATING CENTER HAS A STATE-OF-THE-ART COMPUTER INFRASTRUCTURE AND ALL DATA TRANSMISSION PROTOCOLS ARE ENCRYPTED AND COMPATIBLE WITH HIPAA. SPECIFICALLY OPENCLINICA (WEB-BASED CLINICAL STUDIES DATA MANAGEMENT SYSTEM), EROOMTM (WEB-BASED COLLABORATIVE WORKSPACE) AND RED CAP WILL BE USED TO TRANSMIT DATA. THESE APPLICATIONS USE THE SSL PROTOCOL TO TRANSMIT DATA SECURELY OVER THE INTERNET. \n \n AS THE DATA COORDINATING CENTER, UTAH WILL PROCESS DUAS AND BAAS WITH EACH PARTICIPATING SITE AND WILL BE RESPONSIBLE WITH CONFIRMING IRB APPROVAL FOR EACH SITE. IRB CONFIRMATION WILL BE FORWARDED TO WASHINGTON UNIVERSITY. IN ADDITION, THE DCC WILL WORK DIRECTLY WITH THE WU PRINCIPAL INVESTIGATOR ON THE PROTOCOL OVERSIGHT AND WILL ACTIVELY ENGAGE IN THE DEVELOPMENT OF PROTOCOL, MANUAL OF PROCEDURES AND LABORATORY MANUAL.  ADDITIONAL, UTAH WILL ASSIST IN CRF DEVELOPMENT, SITE INITIATION AND RESOLUTION OF COORDINATOR QUERIES. THE DCC WILL FURTHER PARTICIPATE ACTIVELY IN ANALYSIS PLANNING, INTERPRETATION OF RESULTS AND PRESENTATION OF THE STUDY OUTCOMES.\n \n TRAVEL REQUIRED FOR TWO PARTICIPANTS, DATA MANAGER, AND PROJECT MANAGER TO TRAVEL TO THE STUDY TRAINING SITE (AS BUDGETED).",
